 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. A scroll for «الكلم» (leaving before their words), scales for «بالقسط» (justice, not the Mizan). Their instruction «إن أوتيتم هذا فخذوه…» (41:32-40) is not glossed. Al-Muyassar's first-person «فإني ناصرك» not used. STAGING v4: 41: a town at dusk. 41:1-16: three men (the hypocrites, Al-Muyassar) shake their heads on 41:6 (denial), speak to a group of believers on 41:11 (their outward claim of faith) and turn away on 41:14 (their hearts did not believe); both groups leave on 41:17. 41:17-40: a group of followers listens to one chief (As-Sa'di: their leaders; Al-Muyassar: their rabbis' forgeries): he speaks on 41:20, holds a book on 41:27 with the scroll plate on 41:28 (distorting the words), speaks to them on 41:32 and shakes his head on 41:40 (their instruction to beware). Nobody faces or walks toward an empty side; the Prophet is not implied. 41:41-50 (Allah's will): only the camera and a geometric plate. 41:62-63: the followers and the chief lower their heads (disgrace in this world); nobody leaves on the punishment words. 42 stays ambient: those who come to the Prophet for judgment and his choice to judge or turn away (his own conduct)."
 },
